  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">True Cost Accounting Tool</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MVO Nederland was supported to bring together Dutch companies and make a True Cost Accounting Tool. The coffee companies were involved to include their producers in the process to ensure equal partnerships and create transparency within the coffee chain. To make true pricing visible a full social and environmental picture has to be made. The make the tool usable a few themes were selected: living income gap, soil degradation and carbon emission. In the future this will also include living wage, occupational health and safety, access to healthcare, access to education, child labour risks and gender. With this tool producers gain insights in their true cost of production. At the moment the tool is now being used in Colombia and Peru. By gaining transparency, farmers can ask higher prices for their coffee and decide to take measures on quality improvement to gain premiums. Secondly the DGGF-TA supports the visibility of the Tue Cost Accounting Tool and the marketing of the True Price of coffee. 28 Dutch companies have now signed on the project. Throughout this TA 3 indirect FTE were supported regarding making this tool and more than 250 farmers were trained on how to use the tool</narrative>
  </description>
